---
<p>This page covers bindings, conditionals, postfix forms, loops, <code>switch</code>, cleanup with <code>defer</code>, and the checks <code>requires</code> and <code>expects</code>. Attributes before a statement are rejected, except <code>@unobservable</code> in tests (BYN1016, BYN1069).</p>

<h2 id="bindings">Bindings</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>let</code> is immutable, <code>var</code> is mutable, <code>const</code> is a compile-time value. Assigning to a <code>let</code> is BYN2104, and the help shows <code>var</code>.</li>
  <li>Parameters are immutable. To change one, copy it into a <code>var</code>.</li>
  <li>A <code>var</code> that is never reassigned gets a warning that suggests <code>let</code> (BYN2311).</li>
  <li>A local puts the name first: <code>let w: Grams = 0g</code>. A declaration puts the type first. <code>Grams w = 0g</code> in a body is rejected with a fix (BYN1043).</li>
  <li><strong>Shadowing</strong> with <code>let</code> in the same scope is allowed when the type changes. Shadowing with the same type is a warning (BYN2028).</li>
  <li>A loop variable is a fresh <code>let</code> for each step.</li>
</ul>
<example name="ref-statements-bindings"/>
<pre><code class="byn">let a = 5
a = 6</code></pre>
<figure class="diag">
<pre><span class="err">error BYN2104:</span> `a` is immutable
  --&gt; st-lett.byn:2:1

<span class="gut">  2 │</span> a = 6
<span class="gut">    │</span> <span class="hl">^ declared with `let` on line 1</span>
<span class="gut">    │</span>
  help: declare it with `var` if it should change
<span class="gut">    │</span> 1 │ var a = 5
<span class="gut">    │</span>   │ +++</pre>
  <figcaption>The compiler’s message for this program.</figcaption>
</figure>
<pre><code class="byn">void f(i64 p) { p = 3 }
f(1)</code></pre>
<figure class="diag">
<pre><span class="err">error BYN2104:</span> `p` is immutable
  --&gt; st-param.byn:1:17

<span class="gut">  1 │</span> void f(i64 p) { p = 3 }
<span class="gut">    │</span>                 <span class="hl">^ parameters are immutable</span>
<span class="gut">    │</span>
  help: copy it into a local `var`, or take it by `ref` if the caller's value should change</pre>
  <figcaption>The compiler’s message for this program.</figcaption>
</figure>
<pre><code class="byn">let x = 1
let x = 3
print("x")</code></pre>
